    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῠρίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rub with ointment</i> or <i>unguent, anoint</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				938
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
			</span></i> Com.<i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύροισιν μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					529
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>anoint oneself</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				148.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				518.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἀλαβάστου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					62.1
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεμυρις μένοι τὸ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.195
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				190.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				832a4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρίζεσθαι τὴν κεφαλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.142a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in 
				Pass.
			 also, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τινί</span>
			<i>to be fragrant with</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				10.26
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμυρίζω</span>.)</div>
